    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1662">

                <pb facs="1060" n="944" xml:id="pg944"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/2347.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Minister Jefferson.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received and has read
                    with interest your No. 109 of August 19, 1914, reporting in regard to the
                    alleged participation of one Clifford D. Sands, an American citizen, in an
                    unsuccessful attack on the police barracks at Bluefields.</p>
                <p>You will keep the Department advised with regard to this case.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
